  {
    "id": "6d2d6b4fad7e",
    "text": "What if choosing peace means letting go of what feels familiar?\nThe old patterns, the comforting chaos, can be a heavy blanket.\nEven when they hurt, we cling to what we know, mistaking drama for love.\nBut healing asks for a different kind of bravery.\nThe courage to step away from the storm, not into another one.\nTo finally choose the soft quiet over the deafening noise.\nTo build a sanctuary where stillness isn't a void, but a foundation.\nAnd find the profound strength in simply choosing to be well.",
