  {
    "id": "11ddce707afe",
    "text": "My heart learned to brace for the echo after his grandest promises.\nHe always spoke in grand plans, big 'I'll fix it' promises.\nWaiting for the silence that always followed his big declarations.\nAll I wanted was a quiet certainty, something solid to lean on.\nThen, one evening, after a hard day, a small note found me.\nNot an extravagant promise, just 'Dinner in the fridge. Rest.'\nAnd a single, perfect orange, peeled and segmented for me.\nIt wasn't the food, it was the steady, quiet, unseen act.\nThe quiet remembering. The pattern, not the words, finally held me.",
    "embedding": [
      0.022394296451119462,
      -0.022394296451119462,
      0.044788592902238925,
      0.0,
